**C-5df6a315 → `tasks/tarn-quay/`** (medium, data_processing) — merge fragmented multi-format snapshot exports (CSV/JSONL/JSON, zero-padded ids/values, whitespace-padded names, quoted CSV names, malformed rows skipped, duplicate ids resolved by min `(value, name)`) and serialize the complete roster as a JSON array of `{id:int, name:str, value:int}` sorted ascending by id with no duplicates. Verifier executes `/app/merge.py` on the visible snapshots + 4 hidden snapshot sets (empty dir, conflicts/ties/negatives, quoted+malformed, reverse-order) with distinct asserts for types, strict ascending order, uniqueness, and exact content. Scenario differs from juniper-quill (file-based multi-format merge instead of XOR-SQLite recovery).

**C-d7f631d3 → `tasks/ferrite-strait/`** (hard, system_administration) — firmware-stage kiosk VM provisioning: `launch.sh` boots qemu in the background with **VNC display :1** (5901) and a monitoring web server on the **standard web port 80**, idempotent pidfile-driven teardown, readiness poll, plus a live `/cgi-bin/status.json` CGI endpoint reflecting the real qemu pid/uptime. Verifier checks pidfile liveness + exact cmdline flags, netstat/ss LISTEN assertions for both ports, RFB protocol greeting, HTTP page title/marker, and live-status field correctness across the default config and 3 hidden configs. Note: during bring-up I found the base image's distro kernel is unbootable by `qemu-system-x86_64` on this arm64 host (amber-upland's oracle currently fails the same way), so this task uses an arch-independent firmware-stage VM (SeaBIOS under TCG) — fully deterministic on any host architecture and independent of amber-upland's design.

